# Table of contents: In table of contents: false keeps a heading out of the table while it stays a heading.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Table of contents · Headings left out
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For element: TOC 2
			Box:
				Padding: 0 0 0 14
				Margin: 0 0 3 0
	Section:
		Text: Table of contents
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			In table of contents: false
			Text: Headings left out
		Paragraph: A heading with `In table of contents: false` is still a heading, with its bookmark and its level, but has no entry. It is the usual choice for the title of a cover or of the table of contents itself, as the title of this page.
			Style: intro
		Table of contents:
			Style: sample
		Heading 2:
			Text: Listed section
		Paragraph: This section has an entry.
		Heading 2:
			In table of contents: false
			Text: Section left out
		Paragraph: This one has none, but it still appears in the bookmarks of the PDF.
		Heading 2:
			Text: Another listed section
		Paragraph: This section has an entry again.
